 {"id":"fabro-759d","title":"gofib: add -n flag to control how many Fibonacci numbers are printed","status":"closed","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-22T16:55:52.153Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-22T17:21:09.781Z","description":"Extend the existing gofib CLI with a -n flag.\n\nRequirements:\n- Default behavior unchanged: 'gofib' prints the first 100 Fibonacci numbers, one per line, '<index>: <value>'.\n- 'gofib -n 10' prints exactly the first 10 numbers in the same format.\n- Use the flag package (stdlib). The flag must be named n, usage text must explain the default.\n- n must be >= 1; invalid values (0, negative) cause a non-zero exit with an error message on stderr.\n- Extend fib_test.go: table-driven tests for n=1, n=10, and the default path; one test for the error case (n=0) asserting non-zero exit and stderr message (use os/exec or extract the run logic for testability).\n- No external dependencies. 'just qualitygate' must pass.\n\nDone when: 'go run . -n 5' prints exactly 5 lines with correct values and the gate is green.","labels":["ready-for-agent"],"closedAt":"2026-08-22T17:21:09.781Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-a1f5","title":"gofib: add -json flag for machine-readable output","status":"closed","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-22T17:55:44.876Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-22T18:51:51.057Z","description":"Extend the gofib CLI with a -json output mode.\n\nRequirements:\n- New bool flag 'json' via the flag package: 'gofib -json' or 'gofib -json -n 5'.\n- JSON mode emits one JSON object per line (JSON Lines), each object exactly:\n  {\"index\": <int>, \"fib\": \"<value-as-string>\"}\n- fib values are big numbers; serialize them as strings to stay JSON-safe.\n- Text mode (default) unchanged: '<index>: <value>'.\n- Both flags combine: -json -n 10 emits exactly 10 JSON lines.\n- Invalid usage (n < 1) still exits non-zero with stderr error, in both modes.\n- Extend fib_test.go: table-driven tests for run() covering json+n=1,\n  json default, and combined -json -n 10; assert exact JSON lines\n  (unmarshal each line and compare fields).\n- No external dependencies (stdlib only: encoding/json allowed).\n- 'just qualitygate' must pass.\n\nDone when: 'go run . -json -n 5' emits exactly 5 valid JSON lines with\ncorrect fib values and the gate is green.","labels":["ready-for-agent"],"closedAt":"2026-08-22T18:51:51.057Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-0879","title":"gofib: add -pretty flag for aligned column output","status":"closed","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-22T19:50:57.960Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-22T20:51:51.893Z","description":"Extend the gofib CLI with a -pretty output mode.\n\nRequirements:\n- New bool flag 'pretty' via the flag package: 'gofib -pretty', 'gofib -pretty -n 10', and 'gofib -pretty -json' are all valid.\n- Pretty TEXT mode: two aligned columns, right-aligned index and value:\n    '   1:                    1'\n    '   2:                    1'\n    '  10:                   55'\n    ' 100:  354224848179261915075'\n  The index column width is the width of the largest index; the value column width is the width of the largest value. Both right-aligned, separated by ': '.\n- The largest index/value depend on n: for -n 5 the widths come from the 5th line, not the 100th.\n- Pretty JSON mode: JSON Lines, same objects as -json ({\"index\":<int>,\"fib\":\"<string>\"}); -pretty only affects text mode. Document this in the flag usage text.\n- -pretty with -n: both combine (pretty text for exactly n numbers).\n- Default output (no -pretty) unchanged: '<index>: <value>' with single spaces.\n- Extend fib_test.go: table-driven tests for run() covering pretty+n=5 (exact expected 5 lines including padding), pretty default (assert line count 100 and the exact last line), pretty+json (identical lines to -json for n=3). Compute expected strings in tests, do not hardcode F-values beyond small n.\n- No external dependencies. 'just qualitygate' must pass.\n\nDone when: 'go run . -pretty -n 5' prints the exact aligned 5-line block above (widths from the 5th line) and the gate is green.\n\nMerged from run 01M0NJZGX7BMJAJC3CZJZ0RNT0 (implementer + gate green; reviewer died on z.ai broken pipe, transient_infra — human override, output manually verified: -pretty -n 10/-n 12/default widths correct).","labels":["ready-for-agent"],"closedAt":"2026-08-22T20:51:51.722Z"}
