 {"id":"fabro-d810","title":"Develop workflow: adopt preamble stage scoping + budget (prove a85b/facd/6a78 fixes in the loop)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-08-23T10:56:49.844Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-23T10:56:49.844Z","description":"## Goal\n\nMake the develop workflow EXERCISE the new preamble features so the\nlab loop proves them under real conditions — the evidence gate for\nthe upstream PR offer (see companion seed on denkhaus, fabro-29f7).\n\n## Changes to the workflow (assets canonical on meta per ADR-0003)\n\nEdit on meta/denkhaus-lab .fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro,\nthen sync-check must pass in BOTH worlds:\n\n1. REVIEWER NODE — stage scoping (the observed 25.6k preamble case):\n\n   reviewer [\n       ...\n       preamble_stages_ignore=\"planner\"\n   ]\n\n   The reviewer needs: current seed spec + evidence capture (its own\n   cycle, produced by the evidence node) — NOT the planner's verbose\n   response. seed_brief context_update still renders via ## Context.\n\n2. GRAPH BUDGET — explicit and measured (not just the 12KB default):\n\n   graph [ ... preamble_budget_kb=12 ]\n\n   Forces the aggregate pass to be observable in every run; adjust\n   AFTER first measurement if 12KB cuts real evidence (evidence node\n   outputs can legitimately be 6-7k).\n\n3. REFINER/implementer nodes: evaluate fidelity settings together\n   with scoping — implementer may want implementer-own + last\n   reviewer verdict only; decide from the first measured run.\n\n## What the loop must prove (a85b acceptance, >=3 cycles)\n\n- preamble of reviewer stays CONSTANT size across cycles (no linear\n  growth): assert via run events / fabro ask on stage.prompt sizes\n- both edits land when implementer issues parallel edit_file (facd\n  fix now in the denkhaus binary): no silent clobber, warn event in\n  server log on same-file contention\n- current_seed_id/current_seed_brief visible to EVERY node (6a78 fix\n  in binary): no blind re-derivation\n- skill expansion start-only (af22 fix): mid-text /tokens are text\n\n## Verification path\n\n1. Rebuild happens on the denkhaus side (seed fabro-29f7 sequence)\n2. compose up with new binary; run develop on the lab project\n3. >=3 loop cycles or until first seed closes; capture preamble\n   sizes per cycle; record numbers in this seed\n4. If constant: mark DONE + green-light the PR offer on denkhaus\n   side. If growing: root-cause before any PR.\n\n## Do NOT\n\n- Do not sync .seeds/ between worlds (ADR-0001)\n- Do not close before numbers are recorded here","labels":["review-tool-option"]}
